---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import TrustBar from "@components/TrustBar.astro";
import LeadForm from "@components/LeadForm.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "@components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import { serviceLinks } from "~/lib/internal-links";
---

<BaseLayout
  seo={{
    title: "Our Process — From First Call to Forty-Photo Packet",
    description:
      "How a Northvale Roofing job runs: same-day inspection, written estimate before we leave, HOA paperwork handled, one-day install, documented close-out.",
    pathname: "/process",
  }}
>
  <section class="page-header-band mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Our process" }]} />
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl md:text-5xl">How a Northvale job runs</h1>
    <div class="rule-gold mt-6" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-ink-700)]">
      Every promise on this site reduces to a process you can hold us to. This is it, step by step —
      the same sequence on a $600 repair and a full replacement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <TrustBar />

  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-12 md:grid-cols-[1fr_400px]">
    <article class="prose-northvale">
      <h2>1. You call or text. We book the same day.</h2>
      <p>
        Text or call between 8am and 9pm CT and you'll hear back fast — our target is under a minute
        during business hours. We book the inspection when you reach us, not "someone will contact
        you shortly."
      </p>

      <h2>2. The forty-photo inspection</h2>
      <p>
        Every slope, valley, ridge, and penetration — plus the attic where accessible. You get the
        full packet and written findings within 24 hours, including an estimated remaining life for
        the roof, whether or not you ever hire us. It's free, and it stays free.
        <a href="/services/roof-inspection">What's in the packet →</a>
      </p>

      <h2>3. The written estimate — before we leave the driveway</h2>
      <p>
        Not a verbal ballpark, not "we'll email you this week." An itemized written price, standing
        offer, no pressure. If a repair is the honest answer, that's what the estimate says.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Materials, colors, and community approvals</h2>
      <p>
        We bring manufacturer samples to your driveway and quote options side by side — standard
        architectural, Class 4 impact-resistant, metal where it fits. Where your community has an
        architectural review process (in The Woodlands, Township approval is mandatory for every
        re-roof), we prepare and file the paperwork and don't order material until approval is in
        hand. <a href="/the-woodlands/roof-replacement">How the Township process works →</a>
      </p>

      <h2>5. Install day, run by a named project manager</h2>
      <p>
        You have a name and a cell number, not a dispatcher. Most replacements finish in one day —
        two for larger or steep homes — with the site protected, tarped, and supervised throughout.
        Repairs are usually same-day or next-day jobs.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Clean close-out, documented</h2>
      <p>
        Magnet sweep of the driveway and yard, full debris haul-off, final walk-through with you,
        and the close-out documentation packet: photos of the finished work for your records — and
        for your insurance file, where a claim was involved. Manufacturer warranty registration is
        completed on every install; <a href="/warranty">what's covered and by whom →</a>
      </p>

      <h2>If insurance is involved</h2>
      <p>
        The sequence gains a few steps — documented pre-claim inspection, the adjuster meeting,
        scope alignment — and the legal lines stay bright: we never touch your deductible and never
        act as your public adjuster. <a href="/services/insurance-claims">The claims process →</a>
      </p>
    </article>
    <aside class="md:sticky md:top-10 md:self-start">
      <LeadForm source="process-page" />
    </aside>
  </section>

  <RelatedLinks heading="Our services" links={serviceLinks()} />
</BaseLayout>
